From nobody Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fangzhi Zuo <Jerry.Zuo@amd.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 15:12:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: keep freesync_capable for HF-VSDB VRR sinks in MCCS fallback

amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps() clears freesync_capable for any HDMI sink
whose EDID carries a FreeSync VCP code that the MCCS read does not confirm.
HDMI-Forum-VRR sinks - G-Sync Compatible panels included - negotiate VRR
through the HF-VSDB instead, so the clear immediately undoes the HF-VSDB
fallback that set the flag. Skip the clear for sinks that advertise
vrr_cap.supported, so FreeSync signalling keeps flowing and the sink does not
sit in a half-negotiated state.

[sleepy] Rebase of the upstream submission
<20260901191251.2653684-4-jerry.zuo@amd.com>, which this series carried as
patch 1145 until the v7.3-rc3 rebase. The rebase dropped it on the assumption
that rc3's rewrite of amdgpu_dm_update_freesync_caps() superseded its purpose;
the rewrite restructured the function but kept the MCCS clear without the
vrr_cap.supported term. CachyOS's flicker-free kernel demonstrably carries the
guarded version. One-line behavioural addition to the rewritten function.

Signed-off-by: Fangzhi Zuo <Jerry.Zuo@amd.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_connector.c
@@ -4010,7 +4010,15 @@
 	if (do_mccs) {
 		dm_helpers_read_mccs_caps(adev->dm.dc->ctx, amdgpu_dm_connector->dc_link, sink);
 
-		if (sink->edid_caps.freesync_vcp_code && !sink->mccs_caps.freesync_supported)
+		/*
+		 * HF-VSDB VRR sinks keep freesync_capable even when the MCCS
+		 * read does not answer: the panel negotiates VRR through the
+		 * HDMI Forum VSDB, not the AMD MCCS VCP. Clearing the flag here
+		 * stops FreeSync signalling and leaves such panels (G-Sync
+		 * Compatible included) in a half-negotiated state that flickers.
+		 */
+		if (sink->edid_caps.freesync_vcp_code && !sink->mccs_caps.freesync_supported &&
+		    !connector->display_info.hdmi.vrr_cap.supported)
 			freesync_capable = false;
 
 		if (sink->mccs_caps.freesync_supported && freesync_capable)
